Exercising Interop and SDM on a Lagoon network currently takes separate tools and a separately pre-funded sender for each. `check-lagoon all` now takes one funded account. It derives and tops up a separate SDM sender on both chains, then runs the full Interop smoke suite and a policy-producing SDM workload on each chain concurrently. The focused `check-lagoon sdm all|block|verifier` commands cover generated blocks and existing ones.

The SDM checks assert policy-independent PostExec conformance. They cover:
- the canonical `0x7D` encoding and hash;
- zero envelope fields;
- the payload anchoring;
- receipt `opGasRefund` values;
- the block-scoped L1 fee fields;
- the DA footprint sum;
- `debug_replaySDMBlock` accounting;
- producer/verifier agreement;
- safe-head progression.

`sdm-devnet` remains for existing Kupcake wrappers and now shares the deposit, deploy and workload helpers in `pkg/sdm`.

Effect on operators: the checks never override an operator's SDM disable by default. `--sdm-opt-in` must be passed explicitly. The check then turns the opt-in on only for its own duration, and turns it back off on every exit it can observe, including a failed enable. Legacy nonzero PostExec `gasPrice` responses are tolerated for compatibility with deployed clients.

This supersedes #23028. That PR's head is on a fork, so CI never ran on it. This PR carries the same change plus review fixes.

Closes https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/issues/22988

Validated end to end with `check-lagoon all` against a two-chain Interop + `op-reth-premium` Kupcake devnet built from registry images ([kupcake#63](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/kupcake/pull/63)). The Interop smoke passed, including both invalid-message reorgs. Both chains produced conforming PostExec blocks with zero replay mismatches and a passing safe-head check.

Review: go-code-reviewer and op-claude security-reviewer (APPROVE, low-risk findings only) ran on this diff. Findings dismissed as non-blocking (please confirm):
- Focused `sdm` subcommands, and top-level `all` failures that happen before the workloads start, print no `--json` output. Before the workloads start there is no partial result to report.
- The default 0.02 ETH SDM funding floor is sized for devnets. On a high-fee testnet it can only cause a false failure, never a false pass.
- `check-lagoon all` has no mainnet guard, and RPC URLs appear in logs and JSON. This matches the existing interop smoke, and the tool spends only the caller's key.
- The stricter conformance helper now used by `op-acceptance-tests/tests/sdm` was not run locally; this PR's CI runs it.

